<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n3073" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ăpŏlŏgus</span></b> ,
		i, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπολογος</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A narrative</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apologum agere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Stich. 4, 1, 32</span></i>
			; so <i><span class="en">id. ib. 4, 1, 38</span></i> and
			64.—More freq., </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A fable after the manner of Æsop</i>, <i>an apologue'</i> narrationes apologorum, Cic.  de Or. 2, 66, 264; so <i><span class="en">id. Inv.
				1, 17</span></i>; Auct. ad <i><span class="en">Her. 1, 6</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Quint. 6, 3, 45</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 2,
			29</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
